1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:05,227
ShopSteward is an AI purchasing assistant for small shops,

2
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:08,761
combining machine-learning forecasting, optimisation search,

3
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:13,972
and a multi-agent LLM layer with retrieval, memory and self-improvement.

4
00:00:15,325 --> 00:00:18,946
Purchasing unfolds over days, so the system is event-driven.

5
00:00:19,991 --> 00:00:22,696
A FastAPI service is the system of record,

6
00:00:23,295 --> 00:00:28,551
work flows through a PostgreSQL job queue served by four worker pools,

7
00:00:29,462 --> 00:00:35,549
and a simulator streams sales, deliveries and supplier replies as a digital twin of the market.

8
00:00:36,549 --> 00:00:42,335
Algorithms compute quantities and money; language models read, retrieve and explain.

9
00:00:43,581 --> 00:00:45,492
Routine restocking is a closed loop.

10
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:50,241
A forecasting ensemble of gradient-boosted trees and a neural network,

11
00:00:50,281 --> 00:00:54,669
trained on Walmart's M5 data, predicts seven days of demand.

12
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:56,901
The planner computes the inventory position,

13
00:00:57,834 --> 00:01:02,252
filters candidate quantities by cash floor, minimum order and pack size,

14
00:01:02,905 --> 00:01:05,842
and selects the smallest one that closes the gap.

15
00:01:06,407 --> 00:01:10,487
Every sale, demand change or delivery triggers re-planning,

16
00:01:10,882 --> 00:01:13,693
and each plan goes to the owner for approval.

17
00:01:14,903 --> 00:01:19,071
When a supplier fails, a recovery solver runs simulation-based optimisation:

18
00:01:20,008 --> 00:01:23,240
it simulates stock and sales for every candidate order

19
00:01:23,472 --> 00:01:27,637
and ranks them by lost sales, cost and leftover stock.

20
00:01:28,378 --> 00:01:31,039
Offers come from an orchestrator–worker pipeline.

21
00:01:31,744 --> 00:01:34,422
The orchestrator turns the shortfall into a brief

22
00:01:34,462 --> 00:01:37,182
and fans out one ReAct agent per supplier,

23
00:01:37,397 --> 00:01:43,589
which reads that supplier's documents and returns a structured quote card citing its sources.

24
00:01:44,482 --> 00:01:49,033
A verifier checks every citation and escalates failures to a stronger model.

25
00:01:49,212 --> 00:01:56,888
With a small model, per-supplier isolation raised card accuracy from 21 to 33 of 42.

26
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:01,357
Explanations come from a configurable expert team.

27
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:08,019
Evidence, impact and options agents emit typed claims linked to solver evidence,

28
00:02:08,757 --> 00:02:12,008
and code merges them, under four orchestration modes,

29
00:02:12,705 --> 00:02:16,513
from a fixed pipeline to an adaptive team with an arbiter.

30
00:02:17,173 --> 00:02:21,017
The fixed pipeline scored 23 of 24 and is the default.

31
00:02:22,228 --> 00:02:26,887
The agent runtime is a LangGraph state machine built for human-in-the-loop work,

32
00:02:27,387 --> 00:02:28,495
checkpointing every step.

33
00:02:29,419 --> 00:02:32,903
When the agent needs the owner's input, the graph raises an interrupt,

34
00:02:33,552 --> 00:02:37,009
and the owner's answer resumes the run from the same state.

35
00:02:37,049 --> 00:02:41,201
Plan changes the agent proposes enter the owner's approval queue,

36
00:02:41,415 --> 00:02:47,793
and with follow-up on, the agent starts a new run whenever the business state changes.

37
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:52,322
Each model call assembles its context in four layers:

38
00:02:53,085 --> 00:02:53,625
system instructions;

39
00:02:53,925 --> 00:02:58,773
a separate data block with memory, learned skills and required evidence;

40
00:02:59,403 --> 00:03:04,603
a task frame that parses the owner's constraints into typed fields with their source quote;

41
00:03:05,343 --> 00:03:09,870
and the conversation, keeping every user message and recent answers within budget.

42
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:13,320
Live business data arrives through tool calls,

43
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:17,745
and every call logs a manifest of what was included or dropped.

44
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:22,497
For documents, we built a hybrid, agentic RAG.

45
00:03:23,627 --> 00:03:27,445
Files are parsed by structure into chunks that remember their parent section.

46
00:03:28,565 --> 00:03:30,965
Each query searches three ways at once:

47
00:03:31,655 --> 00:03:35,224
keywords with BM25, meaning with Qwen3 embeddings,

48
00:03:35,364 --> 00:03:37,791
and a knowledge graph of business relations.

49
00:03:38,661 --> 00:03:41,651
Reciprocal Rank Fusion merges the three rankings,

50
00:03:41,691 --> 00:03:45,959
and small-to-big expansion adds the surrounding text of each hit.

51
00:03:46,519 --> 00:03:52,529
The agent calls retrieval as a tool, chooses its own query, and cites every passage it uses.

52
00:03:53,809 --> 00:03:56,719
The ordering decision is a restricted policy:

53
00:03:57,648 --> 00:04:02,631
from the request and the current plan, choose one of five actions with exact arguments.

54
00:04:03,351 --> 00:04:05,411
We post-trained Qwen3-8B for it:

55
00:04:05,911 --> 00:04:10,908
LoRA fine-tuning on verified demonstrations, then GRPO with verifiable rewards.

56
00:04:11,678 --> 00:04:13,988
For each task the model samples four answers,

57
00:04:14,268 --> 00:04:17,895
each executed in its own sandboxed copy of the backend.

58
00:04:18,585 --> 00:04:23,561
Reaching the correct end state scores plus one, a forbidden action minus one,

59
00:04:24,031 --> 00:04:26,231
and each answer learns relative to its group.

60
00:04:27,371 --> 00:04:31,388
Without retraining, GEPA evolves our versioned prompt bundles:

61
00:04:31,508 --> 00:04:35,350
a reflection model reads failed runs, rewrites the prompt,

62
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:38,552
and keeps a Pareto frontier of the best versions,

63
00:04:39,184 --> 00:04:44,284
lifting expert accuracy from 18 to 22 of 24 on unseen cases.

64
00:04:45,031 --> 00:04:49,371
A learning worker distils the owner's repeated operations into reusable skills,

65
00:04:50,057 --> 00:04:51,797
retrieved when their preconditions match.
